Chapter 3: Fundamental Principle

Central Hypothesis. Every proposition possesses a measurable accreditation state that evolves continuously according to the available evidence. Accreditation is distinct from truth: truth is a property of reality, while accreditation quantifies evidential support.

This separation permits the framework to operate under irreducible uncertainty, as is typical in real information environments.

